<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
<meta charset="utf-8">
<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1">
<title>Toronto Street Names &mdash; Changes Per City Release</title>
<link rel="stylesheet" href="index.css">
<style>
  main { max-width: 900px; }
  .legend { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 1.1rem; font-size: .9rem; margin: 1rem 0 .25rem; }
  .legend span { display: inline-flex; align-items: center; gap: .4rem; }
  .legend i { display: inline-block; width: 18px; height: 0; border-top: 2px solid; border-radius: 2px; }
  .chart { position: relative; overflow-x: auto; }
  .chart svg { display: block; width: 100%; min-width: 640px; height: auto; font-size: 12px; }
  .chart .grid { stroke: var(--border); stroke-width: 1; }
  .chart .axis { fill: var(--muted); }
  .chart .series { fill: none; stroke-width: 2; stroke-linejoin: round; stroke-linecap: round; }
  .chart .pt { stroke: #fff; stroke-width: 2; }
  .chart .end-label { fill: var(--ink); font-weight: 600; }
  .chart .crosshair { stroke: var(--muted); stroke-width: 1; pointer-events: none; }
  .chart .hit { fill: transparent; cursor: crosshair; }
  .tip {
    position: absolute; top: 0; left: 0; pointer-events: none; display: none;
    background: #fff; border: 1px solid var(--border); border-radius: 4px;
    box-shadow: 0 2px 8px rgba(0,0,0,.12); padding: .45rem .65rem;
    font-size: .85rem; line-height: 1.45; white-space: nowrap;
  }
  .tip .d { color: var(--muted); }
  .tip i { display: inline-block; width: 12px; border-top: 2px solid; margin-right: .4rem; vertical-align: middle; }
  .tip strong { display: inline-block; min-width: 3em; }
  .empty { color: var(--muted); padding: 2rem 0; }
  table.runs { font-size: .9rem; }
  table.runs th { width: auto; }
  table.runs td.n { text-align: right; font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums; }
  table.runs td.what { font-size: .85rem; }
</style>
<script defer src="history.js"></script>
</head>
<body>
<main>

<h1>Changes per City release</h1>
<p class="lead">
  What each City of Toronto centreline release this layer was built from
  <strong>added</strong>, <strong>removed</strong> or <strong>renamed</strong>,
  street by street &mdash; one point per release, so a mapper can see which
  names may need updating in OpenStreetMap.
</p>
<p class="meta">{{RUN_COUNT}} releases since {{FIRST_DATE}} &middot; page built {{BUILD_DATE}} &middot;
  <a href="./">the layer</a> &middot; <a href="history.jsonl">data (JSONL)</a></p>

<div class="legend" id="legend"></div>
<div class="chart" id="chart"><div class="tip" id="tip"></div></div>

<p class="meta" style="margin-top:.75rem">
  A <em>street</em> is one TCL linear name (<code>LINEAR_NAME_ID</code>) among
  the named segments this layer keeps; each change is counted against the
  previous release on record, so a gap between releases folds several of the
  City's updates into one point. Dates are the City's release dates, not build
  dates. Releases marked <em>archive</em> were measured afterwards from the
  file that build downloaded. Per-class segment counts are in the JSONL.
</p>

<h2>Every release</h2>
<table class="runs">
  <thead>
    <tr><th>Release</th><th>Segments</th><th>Streets</th><th>Names</th>
        <th>Added</th><th>Removed</th><th>Renamed</th><th>What changed</th><th>Recorded</th></tr>
  </thead>
  <tbody>
{{HISTORY_ROWS}}
  </tbody>
</table>

<p class="meta" style="margin-top:2rem">
  Built by <a href="https://github.com/{{GITHUB_REPO}}">{{GITHUB_REPO}}</a>.
  Street data &copy; City of Toronto, published under the
  <a href="{{LICENSE_URL}}">Open Government Licence &ndash; Toronto</a>.
</p>

<script type="application/json" id="history-data">{{HISTORY_JSON}}</script>
</main>
</body>
</html>
